WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.610
- All right, let's finish
up with something super fun.

00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:04.230
Ripped from the pages of social media,

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.339
this is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:08.280
(upbeat music)

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.470
As you might know, the Houston Astros

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:12.205
won the World Series last week.

00:00:12.205 --> 00:00:13.619
(audience cheers)

00:00:13.619 --> 00:00:16.140
It's clear, when it comes to team sports,

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.010
every member of the
club plays a vital role.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:21.030
So I wanna tell you
about a special teammate

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:23.610
on the Durham Bulls Minor League team.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.220
His job is to grab the bats from the field

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.780
after each at-bat.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:31.743
Check out Ripken the Bat Dog in action.

00:00:31.743 --> 00:00:33.362
(baseball hit)

00:00:33.362 --> 00:00:35.945
(crowd cheers)

00:00:41.119 --> 00:00:44.286
(crowd cheers louder)

00:00:46.311 --> 00:00:49.160
(game announcer over speaker)

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.970
(audience applauses)

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:52.230
- Now I can get into sports

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.940
when it comes to that. That's amazing.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.280
I love that. We have
Ripken on the line now

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.930
along with his owner, Michael,

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:00.870
and the Assistant GM for
the Durham Bulls, Chip.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.366
They watch on W-R-A-L TV at two.

00:01:03.366 --> 00:01:04.620
(audience cheers)

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.396
- [Kelly] What's up y'all? How you doing?

00:01:07.396 --> 00:01:08.547
- Hey Kelly.

00:01:08.547 --> 00:01:10.984
- [Kelly] Oh my God.
I love Ripken so much.

00:01:10.984 --> 00:01:13.830
So Michael, you trained Ripken, right?

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.210
- I did, I did.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:16.860
Grew up training dogs my whole life,

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:19.773
or playing in the backyard
with my dogs my whole life.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.880
And went off to college, played
a little college baseball.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.580
And after college, opened
my own dog training company.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:29.220
And thought it would
be a great combination

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:31.393
to kind of combine two of my loves,

00:01:31.393 --> 00:01:35.100
dogs and sports. And so
Ripken kind of started off

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.710
as just a fun thing in the yard,

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.300
fetching little novelty bats.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.970
And from there as he
grew, the bats got bigger,

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:43.980
and had him practicing
with my college bats.

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:47.310
And we got our first call by
the Holly Spring Salamanders

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:49.650
that led us to where we are
today with the Durham Bulls,

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.240
and I couldn't have dreamt

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.040
that it would be where we are now.

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.750
- Oh my God, it's so great.

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:56.100
I would've been the one losing my mind

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.720
in the crowd, by the way, every time.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.000
Like as if it were brand new each time.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.640
Chip, so you say Ripken
is an integral part

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.380
of home games, right?

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:07.650
- Oh, he's a huge part.
Fans absolutely love Ripken.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:10.950
When Michael and Ripken get
here, they go on the concourse,

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.083
and they are absolutely
inundated with people.

00:02:13.083 --> 00:02:13.916
(Kelly and crowd laugh)

00:02:13.916 --> 00:02:16.080
They got their cards that
they're handing out and signing.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:18.260
And a lot of dads will come up and say,

00:02:18.260 --> 00:02:20.340
"Can I get one for my kid?"

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.990
And we all know they don't have any kids.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.640
How many adults are doing
this for themselves?

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.080
It's pretty funny.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.960
It's not just the fans that love Ripken.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.720
It's the players too. We
have Miles Mastrobuoni,

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:32.430
who went up to the Bigs earlier this year,

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:34.980
but he would come and get
a good luck kiss every time

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.010
from Ripken and did phenomenal.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.510
Good enough to be called up.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.750
And so good that Ripken and the Bulls,

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:44.520
we won another title this year.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.687
It sounds like Ripken's gonna get a ring.

00:02:46.687 --> 00:02:47.925
(audience cheers)

00:02:47.925 --> 00:02:49.860
Got his paw size, I think
he's all ready to go.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:51.780
- Oh my gosh. Well thank y'all so much.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.100
Thank you, Michael. Thank you, Chip.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:54.654
Thank you, Ripken.

00:02:54.654 --> 00:02:55.839
(audience cheers)

00:02:55.839 --> 00:02:57.967
- [Kelly] I'm liking the post right now.

00:02:57.967 --> 00:02:58.800
(ding)

00:02:58.800 --> 00:02:59.633
And that's not all, ya'll.

00:02:59.633 --> 00:03:01.200
Our season-long partner Pilot Pen,

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.000
makers of FriXion, the go-to erasable pen

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.080
of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.450
want to celebrate those
creating fearlessly

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.820
and just creating memories
for fans just like y'all.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.190
So they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars,

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.870
that's $500 each.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:14.051
- Wow, that's awesome.

00:03:14.051 --> 00:03:15.348
- Thank you so much.

00:03:15.348 --> 00:03:17.160
- All right, make sure
and give Ripken a bone

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:18.772
or something with that.

00:03:18.772 --> 00:03:20.467
Thank you guys so much.

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:21.562
(audience cheers)

00:03:21.562 --> 00:03:23.013
Thank you to all our guests today

00:03:23.013 --> 00:03:24.856
Luke Grimes, Wes Bentley, Walker Hayes,

00:03:24.856 --> 00:03:25.884
Dominique, and Tove.

00:03:25.884 --> 00:03:27.345
Y'all have a great day, and if it's not,

00:03:27.345 --> 00:03:28.751
well try and change it.

